<title>GERMANY: Bundesbank asks Mediobanca to stop DM issues.</title>
<headline>Bundesbank asks Mediobanca to stop DM issues.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank has asked Italian investment bank Mediobanca not to continue issuing mark-denominated bonds abroad after an issue earlier this month violated mark bond issuance regulations.</p>
<p>The Italian investment bank on November 5 closed a 10-year, 150 million mark zero-coupon bond on the first day of issue and has since added a second tranche.</p>
<p>&quot;Mark bonds should only be issued under the lead management of a German credit institution,&quot; the Bundesbank spokesman said. &quot;The Bundesbank attaches importance to the fact that mark bond issuance remains in Germany.&quot;</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
